 "system": "Louisiana's closed party primaries for U.S. House (planned May 16, runoff June 27, 2026) were canceled by Gov. Landry after the Supreme Court's April 2026 Louisiana v. Callais ruling; a new map was signed May 29, 2026. All candidates of every party now run on one open ('jungle') ballot on November 3, 2026; a candidate with a majority wins outright, otherwise the top two meet in a December 12, 2026 runoff. Qualifying closed in August; 39 candidates qualified.",
